Spent a large part of this weekend refining the Project Ocean website and simplifying the way I communicate what I’m actually building.

One thing I’ve learned through this process:

The challenge with AI is no longer just intelligence.

It’s continuity.

Most systems today are optimized for responses, not relationships. They can answer questions incredibly well, but very little carries forward between interactions in a meaningful or personal way.

That idea continues to shape how I think about Project Ocean:

AI designed around memory, long-term context, emotional awareness, privacy, and user ownership.

Still early.
Still refining.
But the vision is becoming clearer with every iteration.

